        {
          "id": "6f6b0c79-eda9-43bf-a598-7ba4c19bf730",
          "text": "读懂证明",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "58d02253-eed5-42df-b23b-f0bfc1ca8602",
              "text": "逻辑与函数外延",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "ff2fcc49-57af-41ce-830c-d8bccffb444b",
                  "text": "[证明] Iff",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "58d02253-eed5-42df-b23b-f0bfc1ca8602",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nProp → Prop → Prop\n```\n\n**文档**\nIf and only if, or logical bi-implication. `a ↔ b` means that `a` implies `b` and vice versa.\nBy `propext`, this implies that `a` and `b` are equal and hence any expression involving `a`\nis equivalent to the corresponding expression with `b` instead.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "inductive"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "560adaa5-acd9-4bd7-917e-71b0562a9e55",
                  "text": "[证明] Iff.intro",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "58d02253-eed5-42df-b23b-f0bfc1ca8602",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** constructor\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n∀ {a b : Prop}, (a → b) → (b → a) → (a ↔ b)\n```\n\n**文档**\nIf `a → b` and `b → a` then `a` and `b` are equivalent.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "constructor"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "6a331b03-dc28-424d-a218-742eca0a9218",
                  "text": "[证明] True",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "58d02253-eed5-42df-b23b-f0bfc1ca8602",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nProp\n```\n\n**文档**\n`True` is a proposition and has only an introduction rule, `True.intro : True`.\nIn other words, `True` is simply true, and has a canonical proof, `True.intro`\nFor more information: [Propositional Logic](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/propositions_and_proofs.html#propositional-logic)",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "inductive"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "7ec194d4-b782-416b-b4c1-bc64d230adc4",
                  "text": "[证明] True.intro",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "58d02253-eed5-42df-b23b-f0bfc1ca8602",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** constructor\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nTrue\n```\n\n**文档**\n`True` is true, and `True.intro` (or more commonly, `trivial`)\nis the proof.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "constructor"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "84bb4566-31bd-4299-86e0-3b30178865d7",
                  "text": "[证明] propext",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "58d02253-eed5-42df-b23b-f0bfc1ca8602",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** axiom\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n∀ {a b : Prop}, (a ↔ b) → a = b\n```\n\n**文档**\nThe [axiom](lean-manual://section/axioms) of **propositional extensionality**. It asserts that if\npropositions `a` and `b` are logically equivalent (that is, if `a` can be proved from `b` and vice\nversa), then `a` and `b` are *equal*, meaning `a` can be replaced with `b` in all contexts.\n\nThe standard logical connectives provably respect propositional extensionality. However, an axiom is\nneeded for higher order expressions like `P a` where `P : Prop → Prop` is unknown, as well as for\nequality. Propositional extensionality is intuitionistically valid.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "axiom"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "555ba2de-a18e-4b0a-bea0-03f0bbc13e8d",
                  "text": "[证明] trivial",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "58d02253-eed5-42df-b23b-f0bfc1ca8602",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** theorem\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nTrue\n```\n\n**文档**\n`True` is true, and `True.intro` (or more commonly, `trivial`)\nis the proof.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "theorem"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "isExpanded": true,
              "parentId": "6f6b0c79-eda9-43bf-a598-7ba4c19bf730",
              "data": {
                "note": "**概念** 逻辑与函数外延（True / Iff / propext / funext）\n\n**锚点** 6 个\n\n**概念依赖（聚焦内）**\n- 等式与同余（Eq / congr）：type 1 / proof 0",
                "tags": [
                  "concept",
                  "logic"
                ]
              },
              "style": {
                "background": "#f0fdf4",
                "color": "#166534",
                "fontWeight": "bold",
                "shape": "round",
                "borderColor": "#34d399"
              }
